Package: harmorust
Title: Rust Native Kernels for Harmony Single-Cell Integration
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Nebil", "Ibrahim", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Rust reimplementation of the Harmony integration loop
    (soft k-means, diversity penalty, mixture-of-experts ridge) with the
    same RunHarmony() signature used by the immunogenomics Harmony R
    package. Designed to sit next to seurust: Seurat/seurust produce the
    PCA embedding, harmorust corrects it.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2)
Imports: methods, Matrix, jsonlite, stats
Suggests: Seurat (>= 4.1.1), SingleCellExperiment, ggplot2, seurust, testthat
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc >= 1.81; the
    harmorust CLI binary on PATH or HARMORUST_BIN
RoxygenNote: 7.3.2
